KW  - Administrative processes
KW  - History
KW  - Nation states
KW  - Nuclear legal frameworks
AB  - The Joint Convention provides that the obligation to investigate, develop, site, construct and operate nuclear waste facilities is the prerogative of the State. Each State will implement a nuclear waste management program in harmony with its history, cultural prerogatives and legislative/administrative processes. This means that each State's program will contain a number of uniquely variable characteristics. This chapter will investigate the various laws and methods for nuclear waste management in various States around the globe.
